# Commit message template — DuskGram
#
# Format (Conventional Commits + trailers):
#
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject, imperative, <=72 chars>
#
#   <body: why the change is needed, wrapped at 72 columns>
#
#   Refs: <short-sha>        # the commit this builds on or fixes
#   Fixes: <short-sha>       # the commit whose bug this repairs
#   Signed-off-by: itswill00 <anstykx00@gmail.com>
#   Co-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
#
# type: feat | fix | refactor | perf | docs | build | ci | chore | test
# scope: settings | ghost | drawer | updater | release | repo | search | deps
#
# Rules:
#   - Every commit carries Signed-off-by for itswill00.
#   - A commit that fixes, follows up, or depends on another commit names that
#     commit's short hash in Refs: or Fixes:.
#   - Subject line is imperative ("Add", not "Added").
